WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.160
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, as promised
this is going to be my Game of Thrones Religions

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:12.540
video. The show has only explained a couple
of them but Martin went to Tokien esque lengths

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.549
to develop faiths for a ton of different cultures
all over the world of song of ice and fire.

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:19.610
So I’ll start with the gods that the show
has done and then dive into the other ones

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:20.610
from the books.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:27.610
Good news is, we can talk about the gods without
addressing too many spoilery things. And if

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.540
you’re just finding me for the first time,
I’m doing weekly Game of Thrones with a

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.010
book giveaway. All you have to do to enter
is be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.610
But general spoiler warning for everything
through season 4. I’ll wait just a sec...okay,

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.110
here we go.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.200
First is R’hollor, the Red God. Thanks to
Melisandre and Thoros of Myr we know more

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.120
about him or it. Than almost any of the other
gods. Very important though. That does not

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.540
imply that he’s the most important god.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:59.910
He’s based on the real world Iranian Manichaeism,
this dualistic view of the world where you

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.989
have the god of light and goodness on one
side and on the other the god of evil and

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:05.549
darkness.

00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:09.470
In the books Melisandre calls R’hollor the
lord of light and names his enemy The Great

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.060
Other. The god of the White Walkers. I tend
to think of the two of them as existing in

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:18.950
a yin and yang situation. Nature is all about
balance. The show has presented them in more

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.560
black and white terms but I’m hoping the
future books provide some more context before

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.960
we straight up classify who’s the hero and
who’s the villain.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.229
George RR Martin adds a lot of flavors from
other real world religions into the faith

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:28.500
of the Red God and The Great Other but they
exists in a dualistic nature. Diametric opposites

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:28.510
of each other.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.600
There is no known date of origin for the dualistic
faith in both gods, but you can consider them

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.760
at least as old as the old gods.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:39.760
His religion is very popular in the east but
has only just started to take hold in Westeros.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:47.590
On the show in season 2 we saw Stannis burning
his statues of the Seven as a way to show

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:59.310
his newfound faith in the Red God. Melisandre
is the primary conduit for how we learn about

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.729
his culture, practices and magic. Most of
what we’ve seen so far involves sacrificial

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:07.869
rites to invoke a blessing or birthing shadow
creatures. Something offered of high value,

00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:12.769
something given in return.

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:16.450
The Clergy in general can be men or women,
but not everyone employed by the faith is

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.620
a priest. Their church also buys children
as slaves called “Slaves of R’hollor”.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:27.919
Those people go on to serve in the Red Temples.
In Volantis there’s a custom to give the

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:33.459
slaves flame tattoos all over their face as
a sign of their servitude.

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:40.459
It’s not viewed as a negative thing. The
Slaves go on to become priests, temple prostitutes,

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:48.930
servants or Temple Guards. The guards are
called The Fiery Hand. Each organized faith

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:57.249
in Westeros has their own form of military,
the exception is the Old Gods. When I say

00:02:57.249 --> 00:03:00.419
organized I’m talking about the more modern
religions.

00:03:00.419 --> 00:03:03.769
There are 7 known temples so far. Mostly in
the east, the biggest one is in Lys.

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:10.370
The reason Melisandre and Thoros don’t have
face tattoos is probably because they didn’t

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:14.790
live in Volantis.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:21.409
Hopefully in Season 5 we’ll get a look at
some of the tattooed priests. Even though

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:24.900
it’s only a custom in volantis that doesn’t
mean those clergymen don’t travel around.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.930
There are some really interesting characters
but we don’t know if the show will cut them

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:32.400
out. Once they finish filming I’ll talk
a little more about them. Of all the religions

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.480
in the series. The Red God is one of my favorite.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:43.650
As the story continues the religions themselves
become much bigger characters, there was actually

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:50.199
a scene that the show was trying to film in
Dubrovnik near a church. In real life the

00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:53.400
local leadership denied them a filming permit
because they thought the scene was going to

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.089
be too obscene.

00:03:54.089 --> 00:03:56.699
That’s a whole other story, it’s a big
book scene. So if you have read ahead and

00:03:56.699 --> 00:04:03.699
want to talk about it just use spoiler tags
in the comments.

00:04:04.779 --> 00:04:09.479
But in general we start to see more influence
from the various religions, just like the

00:04:09.479 --> 00:04:14.999
Iron Bank of Braavos became a big character
in Season 4. The religions are all just as

00:04:14.999 --> 00:04:21.999
powerful, with the Red God’s church being
one of the bigger groups.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:28.880
So we’ve seen a little of what powers R’hollor
grants the priests, like visions in flames,

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:34.870
blessing the outcome of encounters or battles.
Shadow puppets and resurrection.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.680
The visions that Melisandre sees aren’t
exactly like the visions that Daenerys has

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:43.590
in the house of the undying. Melisandre’s
are more like messages from the Red God. Which

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:47.560
are still subject to her interpretation. When
she sees something, there is potential for

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.980
error.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:54.990
For instance, she tells Stannis that she has
seen he is Azor Ahai, the Red God’s christ-like

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:58.700
figure. But in reality, she’s still searching
for him. And the person she actually sees

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:04.270
in the flames when looking for Azor Ahai is
someone else. I think it’s just evidence

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.160
that the red priests are every bit as normal
as any of the other characters. Thoros is

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.650
a total drunk to boot.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:17.650
And Red Priests are known to disagree. So
even if Melisandre claims she’s found Azor

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:25.220
Ahai, another priest could name someone totally
different.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:32.220
Next is The Great Other, even though he’s
presented as the evil half of dueling gods.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.710
There are theories that he’s not the antagonist
of the series. It’s possible that if a final

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.800
battle between fire and ice ever comes to
pass that the forces of the Red God could

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:51.450
be the villains. I did a whole video on that
that I’ll link in the description.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.490
But the only known followers of the Great
Other are the White Walkers, they’re also

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:59.650
just called the Others, which Melisandre says
they’re his Cold Children. Which makes you

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:04.540
think about the Children of the Forest. There
is another rumor that the Three eye Raven,

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:10.040
the person we saw in the finale. Is aligned
with the forces of the Great Other. But all

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:17.040
this comes from visions and is subject to
interpretation.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:23.160
The Others are known to have appeared at least
8000 years before Aegon’s Conquest. There

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:26.950
has been no indication that they have any
form of hierarchy, but the show supposedly

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:33.950
did the Night’s King. Although there’s
some debate as to whether this was an error.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:40.870
As they have no official organized religion,
you can think of them as more of a species.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:44.590
If you look at what the show presented, it
appears that white walkers turn humans to

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:49.340
their power as children and as adults, they
simply kill people and reanimate their corpses

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.220
to be used as infantry.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:58.220
Next up are the Old Gods, also known as the
Gods of the forest. As similar as a lot of

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:08.530
these deities sound. I think that most of
them are distinct. Even though not all of

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:09.200
them might exist.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.900
There isn’t really an organized church for
the Old Gods, but there are customs that have

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.340
been passed down. The closest thing to clerics
and priests they have are the Children of

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:22.340
the Forest and the greenseers who we’ve
only just met on the show. We don’t know

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:30.090
how many of them are still alive. But 
most of the humans who worship the Old Gods
are from the north, like the Free Folk and

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.830
the Starks.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.810
There aren’t a lot of ceremonies beyond
saying prayers to heart trees, which used

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.940
to exist in some of the castles in westeros.
Heart trees are just weirwoods with the faces

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:56.940
carved on to them. It’s believed that the
trees are the old gods who have died and become

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:05.160
part of the greater godswood. Which is the
massive interconnected root system.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:10.020
You kind of get a glimpse at this when they
travel into the cave of the three eyed raven

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:10.900
in the finale. The massive root system implies
that all of the weirwoods or heart trees are

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.650
I don’t know how much of Bran’s story
they’re going to show next season but hopefully

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:18.690
those scenes will explain a little bit more
about the power of the old gods. Which may

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:24.919
or may not be connected to the great other
and r’hollor.

00:08:24.919 --> 00:08:29.260
In Westeros, they were the primary faith until
the Andals invaded and brought the Faith of

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:33.430
The Seven. I guess you could think of that
as being like the catholic crusades. Although

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.709
the Andals appear to have been far more successful
in taking over and converting the first men

00:08:37.709 --> 00:08:42.379
than the catholics were with Islam.
Since the Andal invasion, most of the weirwoods

00:08:42.379 --> 00:08:48.079
in the south have been cut down and thus the
old gods have no power there anymore.

00:08:48.079 --> 00:08:54.999
The Faith of the Seven will be very important
in Season 5. They just cast the High Septon,

00:08:54.999 --> 00:08:58.769
who’s like the Pope of their faith. Imagine
the religion as looking like the greek or

00:08:58.769 --> 00:09:04.649
roman pantheon of many gods but working more
like modern christianity in terms of organized

00:09:04.649 --> 00:09:05.029
worship. Since it’s the religion of the
crown, most other citizens of westeros practice

00:09:05.029 --> 00:09:05.089
it too.

00:09:05.089 --> 00:09:08.230
There are seven gods, but people who worship
the seven can say prayers to any of them based

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.829
on what they’re praying for.

00:09:09.829 --> 00:09:13.509
Theres The Father, who represents judgement,
he’s depicted as a bearded man carrying

00:09:13.509 --> 00:09:16.279
scales. People pray to him for justice.

00:09:16.279 --> 00:09:20.589
The Mother, who represents Motherhood and
Nurturing. She’s depicted as a woman smiling

00:09:20.589 --> 00:09:25.170
with love. People pray to her for fertility
or compassion.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:29.110
The Warrior, who represents strength in battle.
He looks like a soldier carrying a sword.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.870
People pray to him for courage and victory.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:36.410
The Maiden, who represents innocence. People
pray to her to protect women’s virginity

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.089
and virtue.

00:09:38.089 --> 00:09:42.149
The Smith, who represents the crafting arts
and manual labor. He looks like a blacksmith

00:09:42.149 --> 00:09:46.600
carrying a hammer. He’s prayed to when work
is being done or things are being built.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.740
The Crone, who represents wisdom. She looks
like an old woman carrying a lantern. People

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.339
pray to her for guidance.

00:09:52.339 --> 00:09:57.949
and The Stranger, who represents Death and
the Unknown. Usually the only people who pray

00:09:57.949 --> 00:10:00.800
to him are outcasts of society and assassins.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:05.790
They have a bible called the Seven pointed
star. Seven points for seven gods. It reads

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:12.569
that the seven originally walked on earth
in human form and the father brought down

00:10:12.569 --> 00:10:18.240
seven stars from the sky and used them to
form the crown of Hugor of the Hill. The first

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:24.110
king of the andals. The rest of the gods are
all tied to aspects of Hugor the King’s

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.230
origin story.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:29.199
If you examine it really closely it sounds
almost like Hugor united the andals and then

00:10:29.199 --> 00:10:34.100
people created a religion around him. So of
all the gods in a song of ice and fire. The

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:38.019
seven in my opinion, sound the most false.
That doesn’t mean they are, but when your

00:10:38.019 --> 00:10:41.410
religion is based on a king telling everyone
how awesome he is, it sounds a bit fabricated.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.740
The Faith of the Seven rose up just like Christianity
in the middle ages and became so powerful

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:51.740
that the resulting civil wars caused the Targaryen
Kings to ban them from having their own military.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:56.720
Internally they have a hierarchy that resembles
the catholic church with septas, septons and

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:01.139
the high septon. Their main church is The
Great Sept of Baelor in King’s Landing.

00:11:01.139 --> 00:11:06.269
It’s the building where Sansa was married
to tyrion and Joffrey was married to Margaery.

00:11:06.269 --> 00:11:09.610
There are a lot of subgroups that I’ll talk
more about when the season gets started. Of

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:15.110
all the religions in the series. The Seven
is the most complicated.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:19.959
The Faith’s military was called the Faith
Militant. Which is feature heavily in book

00:11:19.959 --> 00:11:24.100
4. So if you want to learn about them before
season 5. Be sure to read Feast for Crows.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.300
Again please use spoiler tags if you want
to talk about what happens in the books.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:30.740
I know I just said the Seven sound a little
bogus, but the other notable religion in westeros

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:31.699
is the Drowned God. I’m considering the
Iron Islands as part of westeros even though

00:11:31.699 --> 00:11:31.809
they’re technically separate.

00:11:31.809 --> 00:11:38.180
The Drowned God is who they worship in the
Iron Islands. Just like the Old Gods, R’hollor

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:42.209
and the Great Other, the Drowned God pre-dated
the Andal invasion.

00:11:42.209 --> 00:11:47.230
The original Ironborn were a pirate culture,
so their worship supports that type of sea

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:52.439
faring life. They believe that the Drowned
god wants them to pillage and rape and make

00:11:52.439 --> 00:11:53.610
themselves infamous through conquest.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:57.360
The interesting thing is that the Drowned
God also exists in a dualistic nature with

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.970
the Storm God. One above the sea, the other
below.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:07.970
Customarily when a new follower is anointed
they are forcibly drowned. And once resucitated,

00:12:10.209 --> 00:12:12.790
they can go on to become priests, known as
drowned men. Or they can just be normal warriors.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.220
Before theon was captured in season 2 he underwent
the ritual drowning.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:20.819
Their saying is ‘what is dead may never
die’. As they have literally died during

00:12:20.819 --> 00:12:21.730
the ceremony.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:28.730
The funny thing is that this belief sounds
like it developed as a way to cope with sailors

00:12:30.259 --> 00:12:33.309
being lost during conquests either by drowning
or killed some other way.

00:12:33.309 --> 00:12:38.069
The last big religion in westeros is Rhoynar.
Their god is the Mother Rhoyne. It’s practiced

00:12:38.069 --> 00:12:42.480
mostly in the southmost parts of the kingdom
like Dorne. So presumably we’ll see a little

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:46.110
of it when we visit that place in season 5.
She’s the deification of the Rhonynar River.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.249
Which brings life to the more desert climate
areas near the free cities. The worshippers

00:12:49.249 --> 00:12:52.839
their brought the religion to Dorne when they
migrated.

00:12:52.839 --> 00:12:58.679
There is a famous river flowing through dorne
where the goddess is worshipped but it’s

00:12:58.679 --> 00:13:00.939
called the Greenblood.

00:13:00.939 --> 00:13:07.939
Back in the east Braavos is really famous
for having temples and shrines to a ton of

00:13:12.749 --> 00:13:18.879
obscure gods. The most infamous one is the
many faced god that the faceless men worship.

00:13:18.879 --> 00:13:25.879
There’s at least 18 total, but that number
includes some of the gods I’ve already talked

00:13:27.149 --> 00:13:29.119
about. Some of the more obscure ones include:

00:13:29.119 --> 00:13:36.119
Aquan the Red Bull, Bakkalon, the Great Shepherd,
the Hooded Wayfarer, the horse god. That’s

00:13:37.759 --> 00:13:44.350
the god of the dothraki, the Lady of Spears,
that’s who the unsullied worship, the Merling

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:51.350
King, the Moon Pale Maiden, the Pattern, Semosh
and Selloso who are twin gods, the Silent

00:13:53.579 --> 00:14:00.379
God, the Stone Cow of Faros, Trios and the
Weeping Lady of Lys.

00:14:00.379 --> 00:14:03.709
They are filming Braavos scenes for season
5, so they might show all the different shrines

00:14:03.709 --> 00:14:07.709
to these gods. But the show doesn’t get
too deep into the mechanics of each religion.

00:14:07.709 --> 00:14:09.889
It’s mostly likely that Arya will get an
explainer monologue where someone explains

00:14:09.889 --> 00:14:12.160
the logic of the many faced god.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.749
In real life George RR Martin based all these
gods and religions on a mish mosh of historical

00:14:16.749 --> 00:14:21.749
ones like animism, catholicism, polytheism
and norse mythology.

00:14:21.749 --> 00:14:26.920
Right now the Red God is my favorite just
because he’s presented as benevolent but

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:32.360
he seems very sinister. And his enemy, the
Great other is presented as very sinister

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:34.610
but we know almost nothing about him.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:38.350
I’ll still do a Q&amp;A video for this tomorrow,
so please leave me all your questions about

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.160
gods and such on the show or in the books.
I’ll post that video tomorrow. Be sure to

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.489
subscribe to get it.

00:14:42.489 --> 00:14:46.980
My next bonus video will probably be a history
video about the war between the Faith of the

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:48.610
Seven and The Targaryen Kings.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:55.610
Right now you can click here for the Q&amp;A,
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post

00:14:55.629 --> 00:14:59.660
it. And you can click here to learn all about
my favorite Prophecies.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:03.230
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.
High Fives!

